WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.878
Here is the full path from an incoming email to its
opportunity.

00:00:04.878 --> 00:00:07.142
This walkthrough uses labeled training records.

00:00:07.142 --> 00:00:10.915
In Bid Intake, select the message and open Original
email.

00:00:10.915 --> 00:00:14.688
Read what the sender actually wrote, then return to
Summary

00:00:14.688 --> 00:00:17.330
and dates to check the deadline evidence.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:22.434
Check the project as well as the venue before
choosing an opportunity.

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:27.107
Use the suggestions for a new email, or search for
the opportunity by name

00:00:27.107 --> 00:00:29.109
when you need a different match.

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:32.112
Choose the right result, then review the deadline
checkbox.

00:00:32.112 --> 00:00:34.782
Clear it if the current dates should stay.

00:00:35.882 --> 00:00:39.380
Confirm and apply saves your decision and shows the
result.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.528
The receipt names the opportunity, explains which
deadlines changed,

00:00:42.528 --> 00:00:45.326
and shows whether a new alert was posted.

00:00:45.326 --> 00:00:50.223
Open the opportunity from this receipt to check the
saved information in the CRM.

00:00:51.323 --> 00:00:53.550
On the opportunity, open Bid emails.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:57.631
Each confirmed message appears here with its summary
and review result.

00:00:57.631 --> 00:01:00.971
Read original email expands the full message in
place.

00:01:00.971 --> 00:01:05.053
Review in Bid Intake takes you back to that exact
email

00:01:05.053 --> 00:01:07.650
when you need to inspect the decision.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:13.385
If the inquiry is a new project and no existing
opportunity fits,

00:01:13.385 --> 00:01:14.930
select Draft new opportunity.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:19.952
The result opens an Unassigned draft for review
before an estimator is assigned.

00:01:19.952 --> 00:01:24.974
Its source email stays connected, so the team can
review the inquiry together

00:01:24.974 --> 00:01:26.905
and decide the next step.

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:31.281
Project team shows the companies involved in the
opportunity.

00:01:31.281 --> 00:01:34.557
Choose Add company and search for its existing
account.

00:01:34.557 --> 00:01:39.653
Select the company, enter its role on this project,
then choose Add to project.

00:01:39.653 --> 00:01:44.750
The company now appears with its role beside it,
without creating another company account.

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:51.117
Use Edit role when a company’s responsibility
changes, and save the updated role.

00:01:51.117 --> 00:01:54.764
Clicking the company name opens its existing account
directly.

00:01:54.764 --> 00:02:00.032
Back on the project, Remove asks you to confirm
before removing that relationship.

00:02:00.032 --> 00:02:03.273
The company account stays available for other
projects.
